# 🌲 FamilyRoots Platform ("Family Together") — Full Project Review & Missing APIs / Features Audit

**Document File:** `FULL_PROJECT_REVIEW_AND_MISSING_APIS_FEATURES_AUDIT.doc`  
**Generated Date:** 2026-10-17  
**Platform:** FamilyRoots ("Family Together")  
**Projects Covered:** 
- Backend: `d:\Projects\family-together-backend` (NestJS 11 + Prisma 7 + PostgreSQL + Redis + Socket.IO + Nodemailer + Stripe)
- Frontend: `d:\Projects\family-together-frontend` (Next.js 16 App Router + React 19 + RTK Query + TailwindCSS v4 + Lucide Icons)
**Audit Status:** Complete End-to-End Deep Codebase Review

---

## 1. 📌 Executive Summary & Purpose

A rigorous, end-to-end architectural and implementation audit was conducted across both the backend and frontend codebases of the **FamilyRoots** platform. 

The objective of this audit is to:
1. Review all implemented capabilities, APIs, and user interfaces across the platform.
2. Cross-reference backend controllers against frontend RTK Query API endpoints and UI tab components.
3. Identify all missing REST API endpoints, missing database relations, disconnected frontend actions, and incomplete feature workflows.
4. Provide a structured, actionable engineering roadmap to bring the entire platform to 100% full-stack parity and production readiness.

---

## 2. 🏗️ Current System Architecture Overview

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Next.js 16 Client (App Router)                          │
│          React 19 • Redux Toolkit (RTK Query Cache) • Tailwind CSS v4      │
│      Socket.io-client (Real-time Chat) • Interactive 2D Tree Canvas         │
└─────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘
                                      │ REST APIs (JWT Cookie/Bearer) + WebSocket
┌─────────────────────────────────────▼──────────────────────────────────────┐
│                         NestJS 11 REST API Server                          │
│          Modular Architecture • Passport JWT • Socket.IO Gateway           │
│          Nodemailer SMTP Service • Stripe Billing SDK • Swagger UI         │
└─────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────┘
                      │                                       │
┌─────────────────────▼──────────────────┐   ┌────────────────▼──────────────┐
│        PostgreSQL 16 Database          │   │         Redis Server          │
│     Prisma ORM 7 Multi-Schema          │   │   Session Validation Cache    │
│  (base, family, person, rel, vault,    │   │   Token Blacklisting Engine   │
│   chat, billing)                       │   │   Email Verification Store    │
└────────────────────────────────────────┘   └───────────────────────────────┘
```

### 2.1 Backend Architecture (`family-together-backend`)
- **Runtime & Framework:** Node.js, TypeScript, NestJS v11 with Express adapter.
- **Database & ORM:** PostgreSQL 16 managed via Prisma ORM 7 (`@prisma/adapter-pg`) using partitioned multi-schema files (`base.prisma`, `family.prisma`, `person.prisma`, `relationship.prisma`, `vault.prisma`, `chat.prisma`, `billing.prisma`).
- **Caching & High Performance:** Redis (`ioredis`) for session validation, rapid token blacklisting, and transient authentication storage.
- **Security & Authorization:** Passport JWT strategy, secure HttpOnly cookie parser, CORS protection, role-based guards (`@Roles(Role.OWNER, Role.ADMIN, Role.SUPER_ADMIN)`).
- **Communication:** Nodemailer with automated Ethereal fallback and Google Workspace / SMTP authentication.
- **Documentation:** Dynamic Swagger OpenAPI at `/api/docs`.

### 2.2 Frontend Architecture (`family-together-frontend`)
- **Framework & Engine:** Next.js v16.2.6 (App Router with Turbopack) & React 19.
- **State Management & Data Layer:** Redux Toolkit (`@reduxjs/toolkit`) with RTK Query (`authApi`, `familyApi`, `adminApi`, `billingApi`, `chatApi`).
- **Styling System:** Modern TailwindCSS v4 with Lucide React iconography and `next-themes` dark/light mode toggle.
- **Role Routing:** Automatic role-based redirects upon login (`SUPER_ADMIN` -> `/admin-dashboard/super`, `ADMIN` -> `/admin-dashboard`, `OWNER` -> `/owner-dashboard`, `MEMBER`/`USER` -> `/user-dashboard`).

